       TITLE   'Vertical slice'
       COPY    PARMS                Machine-dependent parameters
*
*      Add two numbers in a procedure and print which side of a
*      limit the sum falls on.  The procedure returns by exit 1
*      when the sum is within the limit and by exit 2 when it is
*      not; exit 1 is written as a null, so it resolves to the
*      operation after the RCALL (S4D58 5.2, 6.87 note 5).
*
LIMIT  EQU     100                  Largest sum that is not large
*---------------------------------------------------------------------
       TITLE   'Program'
BEGIN  INIT    ,                    Initialize the run
       ISTACK  ,                    Initialize the stack
       SETAC   LIMCL,LIMIT          Set the limit
       RCALL   SUMCL,PLUS,(ACL,BCL),(,BIG) Add them
       STPRNT  RETCL,PRBLK,SMLSP    Exit 1: within the limit
       BRANCH  DONE                 Done
*_
BIG    STPRNT  RETCL,PRBLK,BIGSP    Exit 2: over the limit
DONE   ENDEX   ZEROCL               End of the run
*_
*---------------------------------------------------------------------
       TITLE   'Procedure'
PLUS   PROC    ,                    PLUS(X,Y)
       POP     XCL                  Restore the first argument
       POP     YCL                  Restore the second
       MOVD    ZCL,XCL              Copy the first
       SUM     ZCL,ZCL,YCL          Add the second
       ACOMP   ZCL,LIMCL,PLUSBG     Over the limit?
       RRTURN  ZCL,1                No, return by exit 1
*_
PLUSBG RRTURN  ZCL,2                Yes, return by exit 2
*_
*---------------------------------------------------------------------
       TITLE   'Data'
ACL    DESCR   40,0,0               The first number
BCL    DESCR   2,0,0                The second
LIMCL  DESCR   0,0,0                The limit, set by SETAC
ZEROCL DESCR   0,0,0                No post-mortem dump
SUMCL  DESCR   0,0,0                The sum, returned by PLUS
RETCL  DESCR   0,0,0                The condition STPRNT signals
XCL    DESCR   0,0,0                Scratch
YCL    DESCR   0,0,0                Scratch
ZCL    DESCR   0,0,0                Scratch
*
SMLSP  STRING  'SUM IS WITHIN THE LIMIT'
BIGSP  STRING  'SUM IS OVER THE LIMIT'
*
*      The print block STPRNT reads (S4D58 6.114): a descriptor
*      addressing the block, the unit at A+D, and the format
*      string structure at A+2D.  The structure's title carries the
*      length and the characters begin at BCDFLD.
*
PRBLK  DESCR   PRUNIT-DESCR,0,0     Pointer to the print block
PRUNIT DESCR   UNITO,0,0            Standard print output
       DESCR   PRFMT,0,0            Format
PRFMT  DESCR   PRFMT,TTL+STTL,10    Title: ten characters
       DESCR   0,0,0
       DESCR   0,0,0
       DESCR   0,0,0
       FORMAT  '(1X,132A1)'         The characters, at BCDFLD
*
STACK  DESCR   0,0,0                The system stack (6.50 note 1)
       ARRAY   63
       END
